{
    "background_story": "Journi was a free-spirited artist who had always felt a deep connection to the natural world. Growing up in the picturesque county of Rutland, England, she spent most of her childhood exploring the rolling hills, woodlands, and sparkling lakes. The beauty of Rutland's landscape inspired her to become a landscape painter, capturing the ever-changing moods of the countryside on canvas. As her art gained recognition, Journi returned to her roots, setting up a studio in a quaint Rutland village. She spent her days painting en plein air, immersing herself in the sights, sounds, and scents of the landscape. Journi's art became a reflection of her love for Rutland, and her paintings were sought after by collectors and locals alike, who saw in them a true representation of the county's timeless charm.",
